  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The\r\nproposal, by reason of shortfall of GIA in the upper level flat, poor quality and\r\nunfunctional internal layout of the living, dining and kitchen area of the\r\nground floor flat and unfunctional access to the rear garden for the upper\r\nlevel flat would create an inadequate standard of living accommodation for\r\nfuture occupiers to the detriment of their residential amenity. As such, the\r\ndevelopment is contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023),\r\nPolicies D3.D(7), D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1 of the Harrow Core\r\nStrategy (2013), policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document:\r\nResidential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010) and the\r\nTechnical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standards (2016).",
    "The\r\nproposed creation of an undercroft above a side access passage by reason of\r\ninappropriate design, scale and massing, would result in contrived and\r\nincongruous appearance that would unacceptably harm the character and\r\nappearance&nbsp;of the original dwellinghouse,&nbsp;and the visual amenities of\r\nthe area, contrary to the high quality design aspirations set out in The\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2023), policies D3 (D(1) and D(11)) of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021), Policy CS1.B on the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1\r\nof the Development Management Local Plans Policies (2013) and &nbsp;Supplementary\r\nPlanning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010)."
  ],
